  "narrative": {
    "intro": "South National for Logistics obligated $275M in federal contract obligations in FY26 to date. South National for Logistics won 52 awards this fiscal year, producing an average award size of $5.3M. Obligations rose, up 136.6% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations climbed from $0 in FY21 to $14.4M in FY22, $43.6M in FY23, $86.8M in FY24, $116M in FY25, and $275M in FY26. The current totals are partial because FY26 is fiscal year to date. The company moved from single-digit millions in FY22 and FY23 into triple-digit millions in FY25 and FY26. The average award-size figure of $5.3M reflects the scale of the individual contracts contributing to the $275M total. The award count of 52 shows how that total divides across multiple procurements. These figures describe the company’s federal contracting activity through FY26 to date.",
